                        <field name="dc_subject">Mortgages - Spain-1853 </field>
                        <field name="dc_title">By Royal Pragmatic-Sancion of January 31, 1768, S. M. a consultation of the Council established the Office of Mortgages in the heads of the Party of the whole kingdom in charge of the notary of the Town Hall for the seizure of reason of the Scriptures of Census or Mortgages with the instruction that was to be kept for the best observance of the aforementioned law... it was used to prorogar for a year plus the aforementioned term so that within it the reason was taken. </field>
